Step 1: Verify Java and Maven
java -version
mvn -version


Step 2: Download the Spring Boot project
1. Open Spring Initializr in your browser.
2. Select Maven, Java, and Spring Web.
3. Enter Group as com.example and Artifact as demo.
4. Select Java 21 and click Generate.
The downloaded file will be named demo.zip.
Step 3: Locate and extract the ZIP file in Ubuntu
Assuming the ZIP file is in your Windows Downloads folder, Ubuntu can access it through /mnt/c/Users/.
First, locate the ZIP file:
find /mnt/c/Users -name "demo.zip" 2>/dev/null


Copy the path displayed by the command. Then extract it into your DevOps experiment directory. For example, if the file is in /mnt/c/Users/YourUser/Downloads/:
mkdir -p ~/Projects/devopsexp
cd ~/Projects/devopsexp
unzip /mnt/c/Users/YourUser/Downloads/demo.zip


Replace YourUser with your actual Windows user-folder name.
If unzip is not installed, run:
sudo apt update
sudo apt install unzip


Then repeat the extraction command.
Step 4: Navigate to the project
cd ~/Projects/devopsexp/demo
ls


Confirm that pom.xml and src are present.
Step 5: Create the Hello Spring Boot controller
nano src/main/java/com/example/demo/HomeController.java


Enter:
package com.example.demo;

import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.GetMapping;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RestController;

@RestController
public class HomeController {

    @GetMapping("/")
    public String home() {
        return "Hello Spring Boot!";
    }
}


Save with Ctrl + O, press Enter, and exit with Ctrl + X.
Step 6: Run the application
mvn spring-boot:run


Wait until Spring Boot reports that Tomcat has started on port 8080.
If port 8080 is already occupied, identify the process:
sudo lsof -i :8080


Stop the conflicting process only if appropriate.
Step 7: Test in your browser
Open:
http://localhost:8080
Expected output:
Hello Spring Boot!

if port busy:
If port 8080 is busy
Step 1: Find the PID using port 8080
sudo lsof -i :8080


Example output:
COMMAND   PID   USER   FD   TYPE DEVICE SIZE/OFF NODE NAME
java     12345 aaibaba  45u  IPv6 ...   TCP *:http-alt (LISTEN)


Here, 12345 is the PID (your actual PID will differ).
Step 2: Kill the process
Replace 12345 with the PID shown in your terminal:
kill 12345


If the process does not stop, forcefully terminate it:
kill -9 12345


Step 3: Verify that the port is free
sudo lsof -i :8080


If no output appears, nothing is listening on port 8080.
Step 4: Run Spring Boot again
mvn spring-boot:run

